implementationPlan.description:
Tests first (DoD 1-3), in scripts/tests/postflight-worktree.cjs. Read mem:gotcha-postflight-worktree-git-stub. The stub knobs WT_GIT_PUSH_REMOTE_REJECTED and WT_GIT_FETCH_FAIL_AFTER_PUSH (task-bc6ba91b, stub :125-216) already exist, so the stub itself does not change. Line numbers are at d1062cb0.

Shared strings. Steps 2 and 3 print them byte-identically in both wrappers, and this step's regexes match them:
- journal pushResult prefix: `push remote-rejected-unverified: ` (a journal one wrapper writes, the other may replay);
- push detail suffix: `; the re-check could not read origin's <T> (<detail>)`;
- replay, origin holds C: `[receipt] origin's <T> holds <C>, the [remote rejected] push of task <id>; <file> kept until that task lands again, which records its row and finalizes landed.`;
- replay, origin lacks C: `[receipt] origin's <T> does not hold <C>, the [remote rejected] push of task <id>; dropped <file>.`;
- replay, re-check fetch failed again: `[WARN] receipt journal <file> kept: the [remote rejected] push of <C> is still unverified (<detail>).`

(a) wtRemoteRejected (:1246), arm 'fetch-fails'. Keep its existing assertions, then add:
- The journal is KEPT. Parse readOr(journal(p)), stripping a leading BOM as wtReplayRemote does. Its targetAfter is c, and its pushResult starts with the prefix and contains "the re-check could not read origin's main".
- The retry: fs.rmSync(marker), then landRun(p,'wt-remote-rejected-fetch-fails-retry',{},{...REVIEW,MOE_LAND_NET_BACKOFF_SEC:'0'}). It sets no stub knob, so it runs real git.
- Assert on the retry:
  - exit 0, and the log has the holds-C line;
  - finals(p) is [['landed',c]], and done(p) maps to [['committed',null,c,true]];
  - the journal is gone, retryOf(p) is null, mainOf(p) is c, and origin's main is still c (the pushes log still has one line);
  - no MOE_COMMIT_NOTHING_TO_COMMIT and no MOE_PUSH_FAILED in the log.

(b) A new arm 'absent', after the loop, with its own repo, bare remote and marker. Write wtUnlanded's 'rejected' pre-receive hook (exit 1) into the bare remote and set both knobs, so the real push is refused, the stub still answers [remote rejected], and the re-check fetch fails.
- Run 1 (REVIEW):
  - origin's main is still main;
  - the journal is kept with the unverified prefix; save C1 = its targetAfter;
  - done(p) maps to [['failed','MOE_PUSH_FAILED',false]], and unlanded(p) is [['unlanded','remote',main,null]].
- Remove the hook and the marker, then run the retry as in (a):
  - the log has the does-not-hold line for C1, and the journal is gone;
  - origin's main is a new C2, not C1, with parents [main] and src/a.txt 'done\n';
  - finals(p) is [['landed',C2]], done(p) maps to [['committed',null,C2,true]], and retryOf(p) is null.

(c) wtUnlanded's 'rejected' arm (:1216): a pre-receive refusal with a working re-check fetch. After its landing run, add `if(n==='rejected')` assert that journal(p) is absent: a re-check that proves C absent still removes the journal.

RED at HEAD: (a)'s journal assertion and (b)'s run-1 journal assertion fail, because wt_publish deletes the journal. (c) passes both before and after.

Error handling in the harness: each arm gets its own repo, bare remote, hook and marker, all removed before its retry, so no knob leaks into another arm or case. Edit with your TOOL-witnessed editor; never use a shell write.

implementationPlan.note:
Harness changes:
- wtRemoteRejected 'fetch-fails' now asserts the journal is kept with the `push remote-rejected-unverified: ` prefix and the re-check detail. Its retry (fetch restored, no stub) asserts:
  - the replay's holds-C keep line;
  - finalize [['landed',C]] and the row ['committed',null,C,true];
  - the journal is gone, landingRetry is null, the mirror and origin are at C, and there is still exactly one push;
  - no NOTHING_TO_COMMIT and no PUSH_FAILED line.
- New 'absent' arm: a pre-receive hook plus both stub knobs. The journal is kept unverified, with the failed row and an unlanded remote finalize. The retry logs the replay's does-not-hold drop line, and a fresh C2 lands with parent main, pushed:true and a landed finalize.
- wtUnlanded 'rejected' now also asserts that the journal is absent.

RED at HEAD (sh, MOE_WORKTREE_ONLY=wt-remote-rejected): "fetch-fails: the receipt journal is gone, or not marked unverified: null"; 0 ok, 1 failed.
